-- wra2-sch.l4: Welfare Reform Act 2012 (UK) Schedules 3, 7 and 8 (consequential amendments).
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively). Part wra2. Host Acts: CSPSSA = Child Support, Pensions and Social Security Act 2000; SSFA = Social Security Fraud Act 2001; JSA = Jobseekers Act 1995.
-- Source: inputs/ukpga-2012-5.txt (a converter script's plain-text rendering; not the official text).
-- Only the text a Schedule inserts is encoded (a new section, new paragraph, new list entry); an amendment that substitutes a word or a number is not, and NOTES lists each with the reason.
-- A list the Act extends is a table of the entries it names: JUST TRUE for an entry named, NOTHING (limited by its own wording) for anything else.

§ `Schedule 3: section 70A of the Child Support, Pensions and Social Security Act 2000 (payment of grant)`

-- src:2959 | After section 70 there is inserted—
-- src:2960 | 70A Payment of grant
-- src:2961 | (1) A grant under section 70 shall be made by the Secretary of State in such instalments, at such times, in such manner and subject to such conditions as to claims, records, certificates, audit or otherwise as may be provided by order of the Secretary of State with the consent of the Treasury.
@ref Sch 3 CSPSSA 70A(1) (src:2959-2961)
GIVEN `the order was made by the Secretary of State with the consent of the Treasury` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order provides for the instalments, times, manner and conditions as to claims, records, certificates, audit or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Sch 3 CSPSSA 70A(1) the grant is made in the instalments, at the times, in the manner and subject to the conditions the order provides` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF     `the order was made by the Secretary of State with the consent of the Treasury`
           AND `the order provides for the instalments, times, manner and conditions as to claims, records, certificates, audit or otherwise`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the instalments, times, manner and conditions are "as may be provided by order of the Secretary of State with the consent of the Treasury"; without such an order the subsection says nothing
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:2962 | (2) The order may provide that if a local authority has not complied with the conditions specified in it within such period as may be specified in it, the Secretary of State may estimate the amount of grant under section 70 payable to the authority and employ for that purpose such criteria as he considers relevant.
@ref Sch 3 CSPSSA 70A(2) (src:2962)
GIVEN `the local authority has not complied with the conditions specified in the order within the period specified in it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order provides that the Secretary of State may estimate the amount of grant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Sch 3 CSPSSA 70A(2) the Secretary of State may estimate the amount of grant payable to the authority` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF     `the local authority has not complied with the conditions specified in the order within the period specified in it`
           AND `the order provides that the Secretary of State may estimate the amount of grant`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The order may provide that if a local authority has not complied with the conditions ... the Secretary of State may estimate the amount"; the power is given by the order, and only in that case
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:2963 | (3) Where a grant under section 70 has been paid to a local authority and it appears to the Secretary of State that—
-- src:2964 | (a) the grant has been overpaid, or
-- src:2965 | (b) there has been a breach of any condition specified in an order under this section,
-- src:2966 | he may recover from the authority the whole or such part of the payment as he may determine.
@ref Sch 3 CSPSSA 70A(3) (src:2963-2966)
GIVEN `the grant has been paid to a local authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the Secretary of State that the grant has been overpaid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the Secretary of State that there has been a breach of a condition specified in an order under section 70A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Sch 3 CSPSSA 70A(3) the Secretary of State may recover the whole or part of the payment from the authority` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF     `the grant has been paid to a local authority`
           AND (   `it appears to the Secretary of State that the grant has been overpaid`
                OR `it appears to the Secretary of State that there has been a breach of a condition specified in an order under section 70A`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a grant ... has been paid ... and it appears to the Secretary of State that (a) ... or (b) ..., he may recover" -- the case is outside the subsection
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:2967 | (4) Without prejudice to the other methods of recovery, a sum recoverable under this section may be recovered by withholding or reducing subsidy.
@ref Sch 3 CSPSSA 70A(4) (src:2967)
GIVEN `the sum is recoverable under section 70A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Sch 3 CSPSSA 70A(4) the sum may be recovered by withholding or reducing subsidy` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the sum is recoverable under section 70A`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of "a sum recoverable under this section"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

DECLARE `Sch 3 CSPSSA 70A(5) time` IS ONE OF
    `Sch 3 CSPSSA 70A(5) before the end of the period to which the order relates`
    `Sch 3 CSPSSA 70A(5) during the period to which the order relates`
    `Sch 3 CSPSSA 70A(5) after the end of the period to which the order relates`
    `Sch 3 CSPSSA 70A(5) some other time`

-- src:2968 | (5) An order under this section may be made before, during or after the end of the period to which it relates.
@ref Sch 3 CSPSSA 70A(5) (src:2968)
GIVEN `the time` IS A `Sch 3 CSPSSA 70A(5) time`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Sch 3 CSPSSA 70A(5) an order under section 70A may be made at that time` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the time`
    WHEN `Sch 3 CSPSSA 70A(5) before the end of the period to which the order relates` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Sch 3 CSPSSA 70A(5) during the period to which the order relates` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Sch 3 CSPSSA 70A(5) after the end of the period to which the order relates` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection names before, during and after the period, and the Act says nothing of another time
    WHEN `Sch 3 CSPSSA 70A(5) some other time` THEN NOTHING

-- src:2953 | (3) For subsection (2) there is substituted—
-- src:2954 | (2) The amount of a grant under this section shall be determined in accordance with an order made by the Secretary of State with the consent of the Treasury.
@ref Sch 3 CSPSSA 70(2) (src:2953-2954)
GIVEN `the order was made by the Secretary of State with the consent of the Treasury` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Sch 3 CSPSSA 70(2) the amount of a grant is determined in accordance with the order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the order was made by the Secretary of State with the consent of the Treasury`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The amount of a grant under this section shall be determined in accordance with an order made by the Secretary of State with the consent of the Treasury"; without such an order the subsection says nothing
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

DECLARE `Sch 3 CSPSSA 70A(7) provision of section 70` IS ONE OF
    `Sch 3 CSPSSA 70A(7) section 70(5)`
    `Sch 3 CSPSSA 70A(7) section 70(6)`
    `Sch 3 CSPSSA 70A(7) section 70(7)`
    `Sch 3 CSPSSA 70A(7) some other provision of section 70`

-- src:2970 | (7) Section 70(5) to (7) applies to orders under this section.
@ref Sch 3 CSPSSA 70A(7) (src:2970)
GIVEN `the provision` IS A `Sch 3 CSPSSA 70A(7) provision of section 70`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Sch 3 CSPSSA 70A(7) the provision of section 70 applies to orders under section 70A` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the provision`
    WHEN `Sch 3 CSPSSA 70A(7) section 70(5)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Sch 3 CSPSSA 70A(7) section 70(6)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Sch 3 CSPSSA 70A(7) section 70(7)` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Section 70(5) to (7) applies to orders under this section" says nothing of the rest of section 70, and what subsections (5) to (7) say is not among the sources
    WHEN `Sch 3 CSPSSA 70A(7) some other provision of section 70` THEN NOTHING


§ `Schedule 7: Jobseekers Act 1995 section 8(2) (attendance etc)`

-- src:3177 | (1) Section 8 (attendance etc) is amended as follows.
-- src:3179 | (3) In subsection (2), for paragraphs (a) to (c) there is substituted “ provide for entitlement to a jobseeker's allowance to cease at such time as may be determined in accordance with any such regulations if, when a person fails to comply with such regulations, that person (or, if that person is a member of a joint-claim couple, either member of the couple) does not make prescribed contact with an employment officer within a prescribed period of the failure. ”
@ref Sch 7 JSA 8(2) (src:3177 src:3179)
GIVEN `the person failed to comply with the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person made prescribed contact with an employment officer within the prescribed period of the failure` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is a member of a joint-claim couple` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other member of the couple made prescribed contact with an employment officer within the prescribed period of the failure` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Sch 7 JSA 8(2) the regulations may provide for entitlement to a jobseeker's allowance to cease` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the person failed and nobody made the contact`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the regulations may provide for entitlement to cease "if, when a person fails to comply with such regulations, that person (or, ... either member of the couple) does not make prescribed contact ... within a prescribed period of the failure" -- the case is outside the paragraph, which does not say the regulations may not provide for it
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): what contact and what period are prescribed is in regulations that are not among the sources
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHERE
        `the person failed and nobody made the contact` MEANS
            `s 46 JSA 19 Kleene both` (JUST `the person failed to comply with the regulations`)
                (`s 46 JSA 19 Kleene either` (`s 46 JSA 19 Kleene not` `the person made prescribed contact with an employment officer within the prescribed period of the failure`)
                    (`s 46 JSA 19 Kleene both` (JUST `the person is a member of a joint-claim couple`) (`s 46 JSA 19 Kleene not` `the other member of the couple made prescribed contact with an employment officer within the prescribed period of the failure`)))

DECLARE `Sch 7 JSA provision` IS ONE OF
    `Sch 7 JSA 20C section 20C of the Jobseekers Act 1995`
    `Sch 7 JSA 20D section 20D of the Jobseekers Act 1995`
    `Sch 7 JSA some other provision`

-- src:3187 | Sections 20C and 20D (uncommenced provision relating to sanctions for violent conduct etc) are repealed.
@ref Sch 7 JSA 20C and 20D (src:3187)
GIVEN `the provision` IS A `Sch 7 JSA provision`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Sch 7 JSA 20C and 20D the provision is repealed` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the provision`
    WHEN `Sch 7 JSA 20C section 20C of the Jobseekers Act 1995` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Sch 7 JSA 20D section 20D of the Jobseekers Act 1995` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Sections 20C and 20D ... are repealed" and nothing else is
    WHEN `Sch 7 JSA some other provision` THEN NOTHING

-- src:3193 | (1) Schedule 1 (supplementary) is amended as follows.
-- src:3195 | (3) In paragraph 10, at the end there is inserted—
-- src:3196 | (6) References in sub-paragraphs (1) and (2) to an income-based jobseeker's allowance include a payment by way of such an allowance under section 19C.
@ref Sch 7 JSA Sch 1 para 10(6) (src:3193 src:3195-3196)
GIVEN `the payment is by way of an income-based jobseeker's allowance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment is made under section 19C` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Sch 7 JSA Sch 1 para 10(6) the payment is within the references to an income-based jobseeker's allowance` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the payment is by way of an income-based jobseeker's allowance` AND `the payment is made under section 19C`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (includes): the references "include a payment by way of such an allowance under section 19C" and are not closed by it; what else they cover is in paragraph 10 itself, which is not among the sources
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

DECLARE `Sch 7 SSFA 8(2)(b)(i) section` IS ONE OF
    `Sch 7 SSFA 8(2)(b)(i) section 19 of the Jobseekers Act 1995`
    `Sch 7 SSFA 8(2)(b)(i) section 19A of the Jobseekers Act 1995`
    `Sch 7 SSFA 8(2)(b)(i) section 19B of the Jobseekers Act 1995`
    `Sch 7 SSFA 8(2)(b)(i) some other section`

-- src:3200 | (1) Section 8 of the Social Security Fraud Act 2001 (effect of offence on joint-claim jobseeker's allowance) is amended as follows.
-- src:3201 | (2) In subsection (2)—
-- src:3202 | (a) at the beginning there is inserted “Except in prescribed circumstances”;
-- src:3203 | (b) in paragraph (b), for sub-paragraph (i) there is substituted—
-- src:3204 | (i) is a person whose failure sanctionable under section 19, 19A or 19B of the Jobseekers Act 1995 has given rise to a reduction under that section; or
@ref Sch 7 SSFA 8(2)(b)(i) (src:3200-3204)
GIVEN `the section` IS A `Sch 7 SSFA 8(2)(b)(i) section`
      `the failure was sanctionable under that section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the failure has given rise to a reduction under that section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Sch 7 SSFA 8(2)(b)(i) the person is a person whose failure sanctionable under that section has given rise to a reduction under it` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the section` EQUALS `Sch 7 SSFA 8(2)(b)(i) some other section`
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the limb names "section 19, 19A or 19B"
        THEN NOTHING
        IF `the failure was sanctionable under that section` AND `the failure has given rise to a reduction under that section`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the words that govern this limb in section 8(2)(b) of the 2001 Act are not among the sources, so the text does not say what follows from the limb not being met
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:3200 | (1) Section 8 of the Social Security Fraud Act 2001 (effect of offence on joint-claim jobseeker's allowance) is amended as follows.
-- src:3201 | (2) In subsection (2)—
-- src:3202 | (a) at the beginning there is inserted “Except in prescribed circumstances”;
@ref Sch 7 SSFA 8(2) (src:3200-3202)
GIVEN `the case is within circumstances that regulations prescribe` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Sch 7 SSFA 8(2) subsection (2) applies to the case` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the case is within circumstances that regulations prescribe`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Except in prescribed circumstances" -- subsection (2) does not apply in the circumstances regulations prescribe
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the rest of subsection (2) is not among the sources
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the prescribed circumstances are in regulations that are not among the sources
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

DECLARE `Sch 7 SSFA 8(5) provision` IS ONE OF
    `Sch 7 SSFA 8(5) subsection (5) of section 8 of the Social Security Fraud Act 2001`
    `Sch 7 SSFA 8 some other provision`

