    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the entries are inserted "after the entry for A social fund officer"; the Act says nothing of any other person
    WHEN `Sch 8 SSAA Sch 4 some other person` THEN NOTHING

§ `Defined terms the Schedules insert and what they point at`

DECLARE `Sch 3 CSPSSA term` IS ONE OF
    `Sch 3 CSPSSA 69(7) local authority (section 69)`
    `Sch 3 CSPSSA 70(8) local authority (section 70)`
    `Sch 3 CSPSSA 70A(6) local authority (section 70A)`

-- src:2949 | (5) In subsection (7), for the definition of “relevant authority” there is substituted—
-- src:2950 | “local authority” has the meaning given by section 191 of the Social Security Administration Act 1992.
-- src:2956 | (a) for the definition of “relevant authority“ there is substituted—
-- src:2957 | “local authority” has the same meaning as in section 69;
-- src:2969 | (6) In this section “local authority“ has the same meaning as in section 69.
@ref Sch 3 CSPSSA 69(7), 70(8), 70A(6) (src:2949-2950 src:2956-2957 src:2969)
GIVEN `the term` IS A `Sch 3 CSPSSA term`
GIVETH A STRING
`Sch 3 CSPSSA what the term means` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the term`
    WHEN `Sch 3 CSPSSA 69(7) local authority (section 69)` THEN "the meaning given by section 191 of the Social Security Administration Act 1992"
    WHEN `Sch 3 CSPSSA 70(8) local authority (section 70)` THEN "the same meaning as in section 69"
    WHEN `Sch 3 CSPSSA 70A(6) local authority (section 70A)` THEN "the same meaning as in section 69"
DECLARE `Sch 7 JSA 35(1) term` IS ONE OF
    `Sch 7 JSA 35(1) jobseeker's direction`

-- src:3189 | In section 35 (interpretation), in subsection (1), before the definition of “jobseeking period” there is inserted—
-- src:3190 | “jobseeker's direction” has the meaning given by section 19A;
@ref Sch 7 JSA 35(1) (src:3189-3190)
GIVEN `the term` IS A `Sch 7 JSA 35(1) term`
GIVETH A STRING
`Sch 7 JSA 35(1) what the term means` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the term`
    WHEN `Sch 7 JSA 35(1) jobseeker's direction` THEN "the meaning given by section 19A"
